  "quality_flags": [
    {
      "flag_type": "unresolved_inconsistency",
      "slot": "trigger",
      "detail": "[trigger_preconditions_coverage] The Trigger does not introduce a distinct initiating event: it restates the precondition that a track/point pair to be related exists and, for the Subsurface variant, that refined information has become available. This makes the trigger condition already true before use-case initiation and leaves Main Flow step 1 (sending J7.7) without a clear trigger action to continue from. (atomic grounding: candidate remains incomplete (EC-TR-009 supports handling tracks/points to be related through an association, not explicitly 'C2 JU initiates an association' as the trigger; EC-MF-031 describes initiation as a main-flow action.; EC-TR-002 says 'subsurface fix,' not 'Subsurface surveillance fix.'))",
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
